"""Human part 35a: the AI controllers' senses: the events of what the human perceived, OnHit, the turns toward
sounds, the distances and directions (game/ai_senses.cpp)

Run with the senses build (build_aisenses.bat, HUMAN_AISENSES and HUMAN_QUICK; the collision, message Read and
ApplyRemoteHit wraps in MUT_LDFLAGS with --image-base=0x20000000, MUT_TIMEOUT 120). Labels: T + the line when generated;
R: lines found more than once in the ranges, with their function's first lines as context. Generated by
_re/harness/shots/gen_mutations.py for lines 44-72 and 414-756 (35b's sight tests and targets, 76-412, left out).

Result (2026-11-15): 236 mutants (213 T, 23 R); 34 not building; 189 of the 202 building killed, 13 survived:
- Equivalent: 427 cmp and 741 cmp (a tie picks an enemy at the same distance: the same human listed twice), 738 num
  (only a negative index is tested), 590 arith (the frames are upright: the x axis has no y), 609 and 610 num (the hit
  message's w: not sent).
- Ties: 588 cmp, 592 cmp, 593 cmp (a dot of exactly -0.4, a side of exactly 0).
- Not compared: 443 and 450 num (the directions' w: a stale local in the original), 704 num (m[4][3] reads past the
  matrix), 729 num (the ray's mask 4 for 3: the harness's volumes answer both).
Runs: the first left 40 (two of them, 704 del and 729 cmp, killed on a rerun with no change: the first pass is not
trusted alone); the queued messages were then compared by their fields (part 33's comparison knew only two types), the
events allocated with stale bytes, the sounds put around the human, more hits on zone 3 with weapons that can be
knocked away, healths of 1 and a position: the reruns killed 27.
"""
